A||||36||Jay||Aurora chip/Northstar||||1||
Z||000000||Jay||03-12-2001||11:11 AM||||Okay WILL, so if the Aurora and Northstar ECM's are the same, the chip from the Aurora should work in a Northstar equiped car, right?  What year Aurora chip should be used, and does the options on the Aurora matter? Are you sure that the Aurora chip doesn't look for TC,climate control or ABS?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Will||03-12-2001||05:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>Okay WILL, so if the Aurora and Northstar ECM's are the same, the chip from the Aurora should work in a Northstar equiped car, right?  What year Aurora chip should be used, and does the options on the Aurora matter? Are you sure that the Aurora chip doesn't look for TC,climate control or ABS?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Have you checked out my last post here? <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008842.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008842.html</A> <P>The Aurora V8 came out in '95. In '96 everything went to OBDII, and Cadillac wnet to Siemens electronics (basically useless for our purposes). I don't know if Aurora went to Siemens electronics or not.<BR>Anyway, the '95 Aurora chip is the one you want.<BR>The Aurora chip looks for the same things that the Cad chip does. The important difference is that the Aurora chip doesn't light the service engine soon (SES) light and doesn't put the engine in limp-home mode if it doesn't detect an input from TC, ABS, etc. At least the Aurora shop manual doesn't mention it doing these things, while the Cadillac manual says that the Cad chip will put the engine in limp-home mode.<BR>Bear in mind that I haven't tested this yet, but nothing I have read indicates that it won't work.<P>The Cad PCM is subordinate to the chassis computer for some reason, while the Aurora uses a more conventional hierarchy.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bubbajoexx||03-12-2001||08:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>Okay WILL, so if the Aurora and Northstar ECM's are the same, the chip from the Aurora should work in a Northstar equiped car, right?  What year Aurora chip should be used, and does the options on the Aurora matter? Are you sure that the Aurora chip doesn't look for TC,climate control or ABS?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>the wiring systems in the aurora are nearly identical to the caddy and you will still have to remove nearly 500 lines of code from the computer for it not to run in limp mode<BR>there is a body control module in the aurora the same as the caddy and also the aurora is 4 litre not 4.6 i have the factory manual for the aurora and in the manual all sub systems are signal connected to the main computer including the radio so if one system goes down the main computer sets the trouble code<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||03-12-2001||11:10 PM||||bubbaJoexx, do you or do you know anyone who can remove these lines in the program.  I've tried several import places but they don't want to touch it.  Seeing as you are in Toronto, you may know someone who can do it.  This is the whole reason why I'm trying to find a ready made chip that will work.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||03-13-2001||10:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bubbajoexx:<BR><B> the wiring systems in the aurora are nearly identical to the caddy and you will still have to remove nearly 500 lines of code from the computer for it not to run in limp mode<BR>there is a body control module in the aurora the same as the caddy and also the aurora is 4 litre not 4.6 i have the factory manual for the aurora and in the manual all sub systems are signal connected to the main computer including the radio so if one system goes down the main computer sets the trouble code</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've read both manuals. The Cadillac manual states that the PCM is subordinate to the chassis computer and that the engine will be put in limp home mode in the absence of signals from TC, IPC, etc.<BR>The Aurora manual states that the PCM is in charge, NOT the chassis computer, and that it won't even light the SES light if signals from TC, ABS, etc. are not detected.<BR>The two engines use the same injectors. As I have said before, the displacement difference can be overcome by increasing N* fuel pressure to ~57 psi. This is easy because the N* has an adjustable fuel pressure regulator from the factory.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jay||03-13-2001||12:55 PM||||Okay Will, I'm gonna give it a try.  If it is the chip from the Aurora doesn't make a difference in performance than at least I'll have an extra chip to fool around with.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jay||03-13-2001||05:29 PM||||Will, I just got back from "race-Tech" (The Fiero Shop).  They called the dealership for me and found that there are  5 chips for the aurora V8 all with different part numbers.  Which one do I need?  Does it matter?  The price ranges from $85-125 Canadian.||||reg||9
Z||000007||terryk||03-13-2001||06:34 PM||||What is the ECM part number that you are using? <P><BR>In the 92-93 system, the ECM is a slave to the BCM. Still, having it jump into limp mode due to no TCM or ABS signals seems odd. I'm going to have a look at that.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 03-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jay||03-13-2001||07:23 PM||||Terryk, I'm using a 94 Cadillac STS chip, I don't have the part number off hand.||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||03-13-2001||07:42 PM||||Jay, I want to make sure I'm clear on this. You are using a 94 STS mem-cal in what ECM? I have a 92/93 mem-cal that I've been working on, but not a 94. <P>If you can call me the ECM part number and the mem-cal BCC (all of the writing on silver label), I can try to match the combinations.<P>I'm not promising anything, but I'm willing to poke around in it more.<P>Terry<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 03-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jay||03-13-2001||09:09 PM||||  My setup is like John Norman, a 1995 ECM with a 1994 chip from a Cadillac STS.  I'll get all the part numbers tomorrow afternoon and post them.  What was inferred by Will is that the Aurora and Cadillac ECM's carry the same part number and that the 1995 Aurora chip will run the Northstar.  It will also avoid running in limp mode.  Mind you my limp mode is still a neck snapper.  I just know that there is more power there.  It's just finding out which of the 5 chips is the correct one for the Northstar.  I appreciate all the help guys, thanks!||||reg||10
Z||000011||Jay||03-14-2001||02:06 PM||||Okay here it is <BR>1995 ECM from 1995 Northstar SUC#16197429<BR>and<BR>1994 chip form Northstar BKSA 1620 2615<BR>That is what I've got right now<P>The Aurora V8 parts # for e-proms are as follows:<P>PART #16208895 Description: PCM(1886BCCN,1887BCCN,3562BKXN,3563BKXN) (w/trans code 5AKN) USAGE:G 3.48R(FQ2),(1ST DES)<BR>PART #16208901 DESCRIPTION:<BR>PCM(3547BCCP,3548BCCP) (W/TRANS CODE 5ZYN)<BR>USAGE:G 3.71R(FV4) (1ST DES)<P>PART #16210105 DESCRIPTION:<BR>PCM(0107BMRX,0108BMRX,1886BCCN,1887BCCN, 3562BKXN,3563BKXN) (W/TRANS CODE 5BMN)<BR>USAGE: G 3.48R(FQ2, (2ND DES)<P>PART #16210112 DESCRIPTION:<BR>PCM(0113BMRY,0115BMRY,3547BCCP,3548BCCP) <BR>W/TRANS CODE 5BBN<BR>USAGE: G 3.71R(FV4), (2ND DES)<P>PART #16217612 DESCRIPTION:<BR>PCM0107BMRX,0108BMRX,1886BCCN,1887BCCN, 3562BKXN,3563BKXN) <BR>W/TRANS CODE 5MDN<BR>USAGE: G 3.48R(FQ2), (3RD DES)<P>Terryk or Will I hope you guys can make sense of this stuff because I am totally lost!!!<P>||||reg||5
Z||000012||Will||03-14-2001||03:56 PM||||I don't have all my materials with me here at school. I'll be able to look things up this weekend at home.<BR>At first glance, it looks like these are chips for different rear end ratios/transmission gearsets. If that's all the differences are, then you need to pick the one that matches your transmission.<BR>For me, it won't matter because I will be using a Getrag and the Fiero VSS.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Jay||03-15-2001||06:38 PM||||I e-mailed Design One and asked if they could provide a modified chip.  They responded by asking if the engine was a LD8 or a L37.  Anyone know what that means?||||reg||1
Z||000014||terryk||03-15-2001||07:46 PM||||LD8 and L37 are the RPO codes (factory option numbers) for the engines. The L37 is the 4.6L DOHC. I'd imagine that LD8 is the 4L Aurora? Someone can nail that down.<P>I know that L37' are the 4.6L VIN 9 DOHC V8 engine.||||reg||1
Z||000015||pherder||03-15-2001||09:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>I e-mailed Design One and asked if they could provide a modified chip.  They responded by asking if the engine was a LD8 or a L37.  Anyone know what that means?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I believe one is the 300 hp N* and the other is the 275 hp(?) N*  I say this because when the engineer that was designing the kit was getting his N*, he told me he could get either so he made sure it was the 300 hp version.<P>Paul<BR><P>------------------<BR>88 Formula<BR>88 Coupe<BR>86 SE<BR>95 GMC<BR>92 Mazda<BR>55 Jones<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135<BR>pherder@kscable.com||||reg||5
Z||000016||Will||03-16-2001||10:42 AM||||L37 -&gt; HO Northstar (300 HP)<BR>LD8 -&gt; Northstar (275 HP)<BR>L47(?) -&gt; Aurora (250 HP)<BR>LX5 -&gt; Shortstar (215 HP)||||reg||1
Z||000017||Jay||03-16-2001||02:14 PM||||Thank you, damn you guys really know your stuff.  I'll keep everyone informed on what I find out, in case anyone else is trying this.||||reg||10
Z||000018||Will||03-18-2001||01:37 PM||||The Aurora chip I bought is PN 16217615 (that's not one of the one's you listed, but that's what it says on the box). Broadcast code BPDZ<P>I bought this chip because it is one of the two which <A HREF="http://www.superchips.com" TARGET=_blank>www.superchips.com</A>  has hacked. It is also not what I ordered. It is an updated replacement for the part number of the original chip I ordered.<P>You need to find shop manuals for both cars. The pinout in the Caddy ECM connector is slightly different than the pinout in the Aurora ECM. Since putting the Aurora chip in your Caddy computer essentially turns it into an Aurora computer, you need to change your ECM connector over to the Aurora pinout.<P>Don't forget what I mentioned in the other thread about traction control.<P>How have you dealt with the anti-theft system in your car? You may have to take a different approach to defeating VATS with the new chip.<P>IOW, this is not a direct plug in swap, but if it will work, it shouldn't be <I>too</I> hard to make it work.<P>ALSO, DON'T FORGET THAT I HAVE <I>NOT</I> TESTED THIS IDEA YET. IF IT DOESN'T WORK, IT'S NOT MY FAULT.<BR>If, however, it does work, feel free to give me the credit.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000019||terryk||03-18-2001||02:13 PM||||BCC year is 1995<P>BCC= BPDZ7615    <BR>Scan id= 7626    <BR>Part number= 16217615<BR>Release date= 01/23/95    <BR>Engine size= 4.0  <P>ECM/PCM: PCM #16180220<BR>Used in cars:  Oldsmobile<BR>Possibly used in: AURORA<P>Options:<BR>FV4 TRANSAXLE, FINAL DRIVE, 3.71 RATIO<BR>L47 4.0L GAS 8 CYL SFI OHC<P>Can you pop the blue cover off the mem-cal and see if there is another eprom under the white knock filter circuit? Most have two small black chips under there, but the one I have here has another single large eprom.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 03-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||ray b||03-18-2001||03:24 PM||||what does Shelby use in S1 with aurora for FI controler. as this is stick and not auto<BR>shelby may show the way out of GM eltritronic mess and into land of power.||||reg||1
