Z||000023||Jay||03-21-2001||09:22 AM||||The Shelby Series I uses a different computer and eprom all together.  Did some digging and found that someone is trying to get the program from the Series I and swap it with the Northstar program.  As far as the anti-theft on my harness, it was removed by Howell when they made it up for me.  I actually never asked exactly how it was removed, but from what I'm told they modified an Aurora harness for the Norhtstar.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Orville||03-21-2001||10:14 AM||||would it be possible to dummy a signal or<BR>signals from the chassis module to the pcm<BR>to keep it from setting the check engine<BR>lite and going into limp home mode?||||reg||5
Z||000025||Will||03-21-2001||01:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Orville:<BR><B>would it be possible to dummy a signal or<BR>signals from the chassis module to the pcm<BR>to keep it from setting the check engine<BR>lite and going into limp home mode?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>In theory, if you knew every signal that the PCM expected. The shop manual only details the TC signal. It's not just a matter of creating a gadget that goes "ping" 13 1/2 times a second. Faking digital electronics is quite difficult and requires a LOT of expertise, which I don't have.<P>One thing I have been thinking about is a "Full Cadillac Conversion" on a Fiero Chassis. It would entail transplanting the Cad instrument cluster and climate control, TC, etc. into a Fiero space frame. The Chassis computer would then think it was still a Cadillac and work properly without any finagling. It would be a tremendous amount of work, though.||||reg||1
Z||000026||Jay||03-21-2001||01:52 PM||||Will, someone has already done this but unfortunately he is running a manual tranny.  He has everything from the cadillac wired up in his trunk.  He is running alot faster than the rest of us and apparently doesn't have the limp-mode trouble.  If you want to ask him specifics, e-mail me and I'll get you his e-mail.  ||||reg||1
