Z||000032||bubbajoexx||03-25-2001||11:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>Wondering if anyone else has experienced this with the auto tranny.  When cruising on the highway eventually my check engine light comes on and the tach sails up 500rpm's simultaniously.  You can actually feel the car rev higher and then the light will stay on until engine is turned off.  Is this the ecm running the engine in limp-mode or is this something else.  Remember I can't scan the ecm because I don't have  the caddy climate control.  It only seems to happen when cruising on the highway, it has never happened at the track or driving around town.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have the factory aruora manuals and if the computer fails to recieve return signals from the steering system controls or hvac system after 15 trys it will go into default mode and shut down the overdrive and converter lock up to save engine power .||||reg||1
Z||000033||bubbajoexx||03-25-2001||11:58 AM||||I worked on a smashed aruora for 2 mounts to rebiuld the damaged harness severd at the left door piller and after all the reading and pin to pin reconects 250 wires there are 6 sub system computer and 1 body computer that are all inter connected to the main pcm <BR>if two or more systems fail in the car limp mode will be trigerd and the only way to stop this is to reprogram the code in the pcm  the main systems that cause the service engine light are steering hvac anti lock and transmisson after 2mounths i got quit famillar with the aroura systems||||reg||1
